# Phase C: Multi-Horizon Hazard, Motifs and Recovery (Gate 2)

Following the updated roadmap in [`.round2-roadmap/updatedone/Phase C — Multi-horizon hazard, motifs and recovery.md`](file:///c:/Users/adity/OneDrive/Desktop/SIH26079-RII/.round2-roadmap/updatedone/Phase%20C%20%E2%80%94%20Multi-horizon%20hazard,%20motifs%20and%20recovery.md), Phase C establishes **Gate 2**: building Failure Memory episode storage & retrieval, trajectory representations, data-derived Failure Motifs, multi-horizon hazard & survival curves, time-to-bust / recovery dynamics, and abstention-aware state transitions.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Hazard Dynamics vs Thresholds Invariant**: Per the failure & rollback rule: *"Do not treat threshold-derived time-to-failure as learned hazard. Reject unstable motifs, future-period analogs, pre-truth calibration, and UI-only recovery labels."*
> - **Survival Curve Invariant**: Forecast survival $S(t) = \prod_{\tau \le t} (1 - P_{\text{bust}}(\tau))$ is monotonically non-increasing across lead horizons $t$, representing the probability that a forecast trajectory avoids catastrophic failure up to lead $t$.

