## Proposed Changes

### 1. Failure Motifs & Catalog

#### [NEW] [backend/app/builder2/failure_motifs.py](file:///c:/Users/adity/OneDrive/Desktop/SIH26079-RII/backend/app/builder2/failure_motifs.py)
- Defines `FailureMotif`: `motif_id`, `motif_name`, `hazard_family`, `description`, `archetypal_trajectory`, `precursor_signals`, `mean_lead_to_bust_hours`, `recovery_probability_48h`.
- Implements canonical data-derived motifs across the 6 hazard families:
  1. `MOTIF-HEAT-DOMING`: Persistent upper-level anticyclonic ridge with rapid daytime Tmax escalation.
  2. `MOTIF-CONVECTIVE-TRIGGER`: Low-level moisture convergence + high CAPE producing sudden evening convective burst underprediction.
  3. `MOTIF-TROUGH-PHASING`: Western disturbance mid-latitude trough phasing with tropical moisture plume over Western Himalayas.
  4. `MOTIF-TC-RECURVATURE`: Tropical cyclone track steering transition near subtropical ridge.
  5. `MOTIF-DEPRESSION-SLOW`: Slow-moving monsoon low-pressure system producing localized deluge.
  6. `MOTIF-SQUALL-GUST`: Rapid frontal passage producing sudden gale-force surface gusts.
- `MotifClassifier`: Matches incoming forecast trajectory and precursor signals to canonical motifs, assigning match probabilities and similarity scores.

